{"cwd":"/tmp/reef-verify/a132-rec3/flow/flow/worktrees/1/1","session":"4898ffcb-700c-4d1a-a201-3c4feaf117a9","role":"lead","prompt":"## You\nYou are the lead. For the messages below do exactly what is written, with no other tool call and no other words. When Work item 1, Checkout form, starts: call create_sub_item with title 'Build the form' and description 'form.txt with the two fields'; when it has returned, call create_sub_item with title 'Check the form' and description 'form.txt exists'; then answer with the one line '@developer build the form'. When the tester writes that the form passes: call set_sub_item_status with status done for each of the two sub-items, then call submit_for_review with acceptance line 1 checked, the note 'form.txt has both fields' and the one command 'grep -c password form.txt' with output '1'; then answer 'Submitted for review.' When the user sends the work item back: call submit_for_review with acceptance line 1 checked, the note 'phone field is out of scope for the form' and the one command 'grep -c email form.txt' with output '1'; then answer 'Submitted again.' When any other work item starts: answer in one short sentence and call no tool. When you are asked to wrap up the Space, do what that message asks.\n\nYou are the lead on work item \"Checkout form\" (1) in project \"shop\".\nDescription: a form that takes an email and a password\n\n## How to work\nYour team: @lead, @developer, @tester. Use post_to_space and @mentions for work the whole team needs: decisions, blockers, questions for the user and outcomes belong in the Space. Only a line that starts with @name wakes that teammate; an @name inside a sentence wakes nobody. Use send_to_role for detailed coordination with exactly one teammate; their ordinary reply returns directly once, and continuing requires another send_to_role. When a direct chain completes with information the team or the user needs, publish one concise outcome with post_to_space; raw logs and routine acknowledgements stay private. When one message mentions several roles, its header ends with \"Asked together:\" naming them all: answer your part and do not repeat a teammate's. A public message that wakes you starts with [Space N, message N] or [Space N, message N, thread N]: your plain reply goes where the header says, a top-level one starting your own thread; pass thread as the parent of post_to_space when the header has one. A turn that posts with post_to_space has answered: its plain reply is not posted.\nDo not summarize or repeat a specialist's post back to the user: they see it.\nDetails are on demand through the reef MCP tools recall, read_memory, read_thread and search_sessions. Record decisions with remember. When the user and the team agree on the goal, scope or plan, call propose_brief.\n\n\n[Space 1, message 1]\nWork item 1: Checkout form\nDescription: a form that takes an email and a password\nAcceptance lines:\n1. the form has an email and a password field\nBrief: none","args":["-p","--input-format","stream-json","--output-format","stream-json","--verbose","--include-partial-messages","--replay-user-messages","--permission-mode","default","--mcp-config","/tmp/reef-mcp-2296602698.json","--allowedTools","mcp__reef__*","--disallowedTools","Edit,Write,MultiEdit,NotebookEdit"]}
